cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use hdmseg in your research, please cite it."
title: "hdmseg: population-consistent surface segmentation by correspondence-collapsed diffusion maps"
abstract: >-
  A fast, deterministic Rust implementation (with Python bindings) of
  population-consistent surface segmentation for homologous shapes in dense
  correspondence. It builds a frame-free consensus diffusion operator on the
  loci, embeds it spectrally, and clusters the embedding into regions coherent
  across the whole sample, with bootstrap-stability model selection. Large
  connected graphs use an edge-sparse operator and partial eigensolver, with a
  validated dense fallback for small, disconnected, or nonconverged cases.
type: software
